attribute: "Supported Instrument Models"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Driver Capabilities:Supported Instrument Models"
	string readonly local 001006D7
"Contains a model code of the instrument. For drivers that support more than one device, this property contains a comma-separated list of supported instrument models.
    "
attribute: "Number of Channels"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Driver Capabilities:Number of Channels"
	iL readonly local 0010065B
"Indicates the number of channels that the specific instrument driver supports.  
    For each property for which the IVI_VAL_MULTI_CHANNEL flag property is set, the IVI engine maintains a separate cache value for each channel.
    "
attribute: "Manufacturer"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Instrument Identification:Manufacturer"
	string readonly local 0010078F
"A string that contains the name of the instrument manufacturer you are currently using.
    "
attribute: "Model"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Instrument Identification:Model"
	string readonly local 00100790
"A string that contains the model number or name of the instrument that you are currently using.
    "
attribute: "Firmware Revision"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Instrument Identification:Firmware Revision"
	string readonly local 0010078E
"A string that contains the firmware revision information for the instrument you are currently using.
    "
attribute: "Logical Name"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Advanced Session Information:Logical Name"
	string readonly local 001006C1
"A string containing the logical name you specified when opening the current IVI session.
     You may pass a logical name to the avr6552 Initialize or avr6552 Initialize With Options VIs.  The IVI Configuration utility must contain an entry for the logical name.  The logical name entry refers to a virtual instrument section in the IVI Configuration file.  The virtual instrument section specifies a physical device and initial user options.
    "
attribute: "Resource Descriptor"
	"Inherent IVI Settings:Advanced Session Information:Resource Descriptor"
	string readonly local 001006C0
"Indicates the resource descriptor the driver uses to identify the physical device.
    If you initialize the driver with a logical name, this property contains the resource descriptor that corresponds to the entry in the IVI Configuration utility.  
    If you initialize the instrument driver with the resource descriptor, this property contains that value.
    "
attribute: "Function"
	"Basic Operation:Function"
	iL readwrite local 001312D1
"Specifies the measurement function.
    "
attribute: "Range"
	"Basic Operation:Range"
	fD readwrite local 001312D2
"Specifies the measurement range.  You use positive values to represent the absolute value of the maximum expected measurement.  The value is in units appropriate for the current value of the avr6552>>Basic Operation>>Function property.  For example, when you set the avr6552>>Basic Operation>>Function property to AVR6552_VAL_DC_VOLTS, the units are volts.  For example, setting this property to 10.0 configures the DMM to measure DC voltages from -10.0 to +10.0 volts.
    Negative values are reserved for controlling the DMM's auto-ranging capability.
- AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON (-1.0) - Configures the DMM to calculate the range before each measurement automatically.
    For AVR6552, When you set this property to AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON, you cannot obtain the actual range the DMM is currently using.

Note:  
(1)  For frequency or diode measurements, this property must be set to AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON.    

(2) This property must be set to  AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_RANGE_ON in burst measurement mode."
attribute: "Resolution"
	"Basic Operation:Resolution"
	fD enum { 10000=1.000000E+4, 1000=1.000000E+3, 100=1.000000E+2, 10=1.000000E+1, 1=1.000000E+0, .1=1.000000E-1, .01=1.000000E-2, .001=1.000000E-3, .0001=1.000000E-4, .00001=1.000000E-5, .000001=1.000000E-6, .0000001=1.000000E-7, .00000001=1.000000E-8} readwrite local 001312D8
"This property configures the measurement resolution of the DMM in absolute units.

Setting this property to lower values increases the measurement accuracy.  Setting this property to higher values increases the measurement speed.

10000 10000

1000 1000

100 100

10 10

1 1

.1 0.1

.01 0.01

.001 0.001

.0001 0.0001

.00001 1e-005

.000001 1e-006

.0000001 1e-007

.00000001 1e-008"
attribute: "Digits Resolution"
	"Basic Operation:Digits Resolution"
	fD readwrite local 00118C4C
"This properties specifies the measurement resolution in digits of precision.

Note:  For AVR6552 series, the allowable resolution value depends on the sample rates as well as measurement function as following table shows:
---------------------------------------------------
|    Measurement       |      Sampling Rate       |
|     Function         |--------------------------|
|                      |   SLOW/MED  |    FAST    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|       DCV            |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|     2W/4W Res        |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|    LP 2/4W Res       |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|        ACV           |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|        DCI           |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|        ACI           |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|      ACV (AC+DC)     |     4.5     |     3.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|      ACI (AC+DC)     |     4.5     |     3.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|         Diode        |     5.5     |     4.5    |
|----------------------|-------------|------------|
|        Ripple V      |     3.5     |     3.5    |
---------------------------------------------------
| Measurement |             Sampling Rate         |
| Function    |-----------------------------------| 
|             |    SLOW   |    MED     |   FAST   |
|-------------|-----------|------------|----------|
|   FREQ      |    6.0    |     5.0    |    4.0   |
--------------------------------------------------- 
When sample rate is set to long-it, the same number of digits as those of the MED are displayed.    "
attribute: "Sample Rate"
	"Sample Rate:Sample Rate"
	iL readwrite local 00118C34
"Specifies the sample rate the DMM uses to acquire a signal."
attribute: "Integral Time"
	"Sample Rate:Integral Time"
	fD readwrite local 00118C35
"Specifies the integral time for long-it sample rate.  The units for this property are milliseconds."
attribute: "Trigger Source"
	"Trigger:Trigger Source"
	iL enum { AVR6552_VAL_IMMEDIATE=1} readwrite local 001312D4
"This property specifies the trigger source.
 
Valid Values:

AVR6552_VAL_IMMEDIATE - Immediate (Default)
AVR6552_VAL_IMMEDIATE 1"
attribute: "Trigger Delay"
	"Trigger:Trigger Delay"
	fD readwrite local 001312D5
"Specifies the length of time the DMM waits after it receives the trigger and before it takes a measurement.  Use positive values to set the trigger delay in seconds. 
    
    Valid Range:  0.0 seconds

Note:  This property does not affect the behavior of the DMM. It exists only for class compliance.
    "
attribute: "Sample Mode"
	"Trigger:Trigger Operations:Sample Mode"
	iL enum { AVR6552_VAL_FREE_RUN=0, AVR6552_VAL_HOLD=1, AVR6552_VAL_BURST=2} readwrite local 00118C32
"Specifies the sample mode the DMM to use.
AVR6552_VAL_FREE_RUN 0
Free run sample mode

AVR6552_VAL_HOLD 1
Hold sample mode

AVR6552_VAL_BURST 2
Burst sample mode"
attribute: "Delay"
	"Trigger:Trigger Operations:Delay"
	fD readwrite local 00118C33
"Specifies the delay the DMM uses for the HOLD and BURST sample modes before it takes a measurement.

Valid Values:  0.0 - 99.999 seconds

"
attribute: "Hold Sample Count"
	"Trigger:Trigger Operations:Hold Sample Count"
	iL readwrite local 00118C38
"Specifies the number of measurements the DMM takes each time it receives a trigger in Hold sample mode.
    
Valid Values:  1 - 9999

Note:  This property does not affect the behavior of the instrument if the  avr6552>>Trigger>>Trigger Operations>>Sample Mode property is not set to AVR6552_VAL_HOLD.
    "
attribute: "Burst Count"
	"Trigger:Trigger Operations:Burst Count"
	iL enum { 1000=1000, 2000=2000, 3000=3000, 4000=4000, 5000=5000, 6000=6000, 7000=7000, 8000=8000, 9000=9000, 10000=10000} readwrite local 00118C36
"Specifies the measurement count to transfer to the internal memory in burst sample mode.

Notes:  
(1)  This property does not affect the behavior of the instrument if the sample mode is not set to burst mode.
(2)  This property is supported only by AVR6552.
1000 1000

2000 2000

3000 3000

4000 4000

5000 5000

6000 6000

7000 7000

8000 8000

9000 9000

10000 10000"
attribute: "Delayed Trigger"
	"Trigger:Trigger Operations:Delayed Trigger"
	iL enum { 0=0, 25=25, 50=50, 75=75} readwrite local 00118C37
"Specifies the percentage of numbers of premeasurement cycles out of the total burst cycles.

Notes:  
(1)  This property does not affect the behavior of the instrument if the sample mode is not set to burst mode.
(2)  This property is supported only by AVR6552.
0 0

25 25

50 50

75 75"
attribute: "AC Maximum Frequency"
	"AC Measurements:AC Maximum Frequency"
	fD readwrite local 001312D7
"Specifies the maximum frequency component of the input signal for AC measurements. The value of this property affects instrument behavior only when you set the avr6552>>Basic Operation>>Function property to one of the following values:

AVR6552_VAL_AC_VOLTS
AVR6552_VAL_AC_CURRENT
AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_VOLTS
AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_CURRENT
    
"
attribute: "AC Minimum Frequency"
	"AC Measurements:AC Minimum Frequency"
	fD enum { 300.0=3.000000E+2, 20.0=2.000000E+1} readwrite local 001312D6
"Specifies the minimum frequency component of the input signal for AC measurements.  The value of this property affects instrument behavior only when you set the avr6552>>Basic Operation>>Function property to one of the following values:

AVR6552_VAL_AC_VOLTS
AVR6552_VAL_AC_CURRENT
AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_VOLTS
AVR6552_VAL_AC_PLUS_DC_CURRENT
    
300.0 300

20.0 20"
attribute: "avr6552>>Frequency Measurements>>Frequency Voltage Range"
	"Frequency Measurements:avr6552>>Frequency Measurements>>"
	fD readwrite local 00131335
"Specifies the expected maximum value of the input signal for frequency measurements in volts RMS.

Valid Range: 0.1 - 700.0 volts RMS

"
attribute: "Low Pass Filter"
	"Ripple Voltage Measurements:Low Pass Filter"
	iL enum { AVR6552_VAL_FILTER_OFF=-1, 1000=1000, 10000=10000, 100000=100000, 1000000=1000000} readwrite local 00118C44
"Specifies the frequency band of LPF (low-pass filter) the DMM uses to measure ripple voltage.

Note:  This property is supported only by AVR6552T-R.
AVR6552_VAL_FILTER_OFF -1

1000 1000

10000 10000

100000 100000

1000000 1000000"
attribute: "High Pass Filter"
	"Ripple Voltage Measurements:High Pass Filter"
	iL enum { AVR6552_VAL_FILTER_OFF=-1, 1000=1000, 10000=10000, 100000=100000} readwrite local 00118C43
"Specifies the frequency band of HPF (high-pass filter) the DMM uses to measure ripple voltage.

Note:  This property is supported only by AVR6552T-R.
AVR6552_VAL_FILTER_OFF -1

1000 1000

10000 10000

100000 100000"
attribute: "Auto Zero"
	"Measurement Operation Options:Auto Zero"
	iL enum { AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_ZERO_OFF=0, AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_ZERO_ON=1, AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_ZERO_ONCE=2} readwrite local 0013141C
"Specifies the auto-zero mode.  In general, the auto-zero capability of a DMM normalizes all measurements based on a Zero Reading.  When auto-zeroing is enabled, the DMM internally disconnects the input signal and takes a Zero Reading.  The DMM then subtracts the Zero Reading from the measurement.  This prevents offset voltages present in the DMM's input circuitry from affecting measurement accuracy.
    
AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_ZERO_OFF 0
Disables the DMM from taking any more Zero Readings.  The DMM subtract the last Zero Reading from all subsequent values it measures.

AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_ZERO_ON 1
Configures the DMM to take a Zero Reading for each measurement.  The DMM subtracts the Zero Reading from the value it measures.

AVR6552_VAL_AUTO_ZERO_ONCE 2
Configures the DMM to take a Zero Reading immediately.  The DMM then subtracts this Zero Reading from all subsequent values it measures."
attribute: "Powerline Frequency"
	"Measurement Operation Options:Powerline Frequency"
	fD enum { AVR6552_VAL_50_HERTZ=5.000000E+1, AVR6552_VAL_60_HERTZ=6.000000E+1} readonly local 0013141D
"Specifies the power line frequency in Hertz.
    
The instrument selects the powerline frequency automatically. This property cannot be set by the user.

AVR6552_VAL_50_HERTZ 50
50 Hertz

AVR6552_VAL_60_HERTZ 60
60 Hertz"
