attribute: "dB Mode"
	"Measurement Operation Options:dB/dBm Calculation:dB Mode"
	iL enum { AVR6552_VAL_DB_OFF=0, AVR6552_VAL_DB_ON=1, AVR6552_VAL_DBM_ON=2} readwrite local 00118C4B
"Specifies the decible conversion to perform.

Defined Values:

AVR6552_VAL_DB_OFF - Disable the dB/dBm calculation
AVR6552_VAL_DB_ON  - Enable the dB calculation
AVR6552_VAL_DBM_ON - Enable the dBm calculation

Notes:

(1) The dB calculation executes a decibel converison. It is functional only during voltage measurements. 

(2) The dBm calculation is useful for calculating the power gain  per mV. It is functional only during voltage measurements.

(3) The db, dBm, and scaling calculations cannot be selected at the same time. 

AVR6552_VAL_DB_OFF 0

AVR6552_VAL_DB_ON 1

AVR6552_VAL_DBM_ON 2"
attribute: "DB/DBM Constant"
	"Measurement Operation Options:dB/dBm Calculation:DB/DBM Constant"
	fD readwrite local 00118C42
"Specifies the constant for dB and dBm operation."
attribute: "ID Query Response"
	"Miscellaneous Settings:ID Query Response"
	string readonly local 00118C31
